ased frame count which really helps  during frantic scenes and an engine  tweak it's actually running on the retro  engine used for sonic mania additional  animations have been created just for  this game and there's even the og 4x3  aspect ratio for people who were alive  before widescreen tvs the classic mode  also has the same difficulty level as  back in the 1990s so if you'd like to  relive the days when sonic was a legit  threat to nintendo and mario then grab  origins on june 23rd on playstation xbox  pc and switch  okay let's go through some free stuff  free games that need you to stay alive  let's start with one which is going free  on june the 1st knockout city remember  talking about this one before we spoke  about this about a year ago and i did  say the game would die without a  free-to-play audience and now it's  finally here this may be too little too  late  knockout city is dodgeball the game  running around on the streets and the  rooftops trying to smash a rubber ball  into other players of course there's  more to it than that with moves to  master and a reliance on timing dodging  and catching the ball are key skills  like you'd expect but if you lack  ability just like me you can get brutal  instead i mean it get physical different  inputs affect the ball differently like  a moon ball which lets us jump higher  and bomb ball which explodes and if you  cannot find a ball become it and let a  teammate throw you instead customization  is the draw to keep playing with battle  pass style incentives after being on ps  plus and game pass this is knockout  city's final chance to survive  so if you don't want knockout city to be  yet another dead game join the first on  pretty much every platform switch  playstations xboxes and the pc  [Music]  now we have a free game which is already  out roller champions released on may  25th another extreme sports game with a  weaponized ball roller champions has a  very simple premise grab a ball throw it  through a hoop simple right one of the  big plus points about roller champions  is all about aggression when you do not  have the ball you can hurt the  opposition any way you can to make them  drop the ball it's a full contact spot  there's a really cool risk reward  element of roller champions every  successful lap of the course your team  completes while holding the ball means  the next goal will be worth an  additional point so do you continue  lapping to win big or do you bank your  shot and get the points on the board as  quick as possible this also means one  play can bring you back into a game  regardless of scoreline there's  something about this which is quite  addicting and just like knockout city  customization is the appeal right now  there are limited edition skins to  unlock for playing during the first few  days or weeks since we last spoke about  this a practice mode has been added to  the game so you can get a little bit  better before you're thrown in at the  deep end roller champions is out right  now on playstation xbox and pc  [Music]  and now another free game which began  life as a full price title four guys  remember this when it released during  lockdown what a game it was and on june  21st it's going free to play and on a  ton of platforms playstation xbox switch  and pc all for free all with full  cross-play support if you've been living  under a rock fall guys is a battle  royale mixed with a tv show like total  wipeout each level more contestants are  left behind because there can be only  one winner the rounds are a mixture of  solo and team-based mini-games from  avoiding climbing slime to catching a  penguin they are so random you may have  moved on from this title but with xbox  and switch joining the party it's a  great time to go back to it june 21st  also sees the next gen versions of fall  guy's release 2 a dedicated ps5 version  is confirmed fall guys is now owned and  backed by fortnite demigods epic games  who have already showed us a new  creative mode is coming which will let  us build our own courses and play them  with friends the battle passes are  confirmed to remain allowing us to  unlock new cosmetics but these will have  two different versions now a free tier  like the good old days and a new premium  tier if you're og by the way you will  get the first one totally free new  courses have been added regularly and  more are coming when this goes free to  play on june 21st i think i'm gonna go  back  [Music]  okay that's the big games and the free  games out of the way but here are some  other premium games you may have missed  check out madison four years ago a demo  released which scared the pants off us a  first person horror game inspired by the  sublime silent hills that game never  made it to a final release but at last  madison has on june 24th we'll be living  through some hardcore psychological  drama being so scared we can't turn  around for fear of what could be waiting  for us we wake up locked in a room and  must perform a ritual to progress with  intense puzzles to solve and the  constant threat of the unknown madison  could be a huge horror title but if  you're scared like me we can watch  markiplier play instead madison releases  on june 24th on ps4 ps5 the xbox's pc  and not even the switch players can  escape this one madison is on switch  there you try it  [Music]  here's another really interesting game  an indie game it's called silt you wake  up on the ocean floor with no idea  what's going on you swim around the  silhouetted world solving puzzles trying  to understand why you are here we have  the ability to possess fish and other  sea creatures to navigate through the  world silt echoes the monosyllabic  worlds of games like outside and limbo  the desire to understand the world you  find yourself in keeps pulling you  forward even though there is no dialogue  to help interpret the information you  receive the further we press on the more  warped the abyss becomes leading to  goliaths deadly creatures like no other  stilt releases on june 1st on ps4 ps5  xbox one series snx pc and twitch if  you're a fan of 2d fighters you should  keep an eye on capcom fighting  collection 10 classic fighters from  history are all brought together into  one game street fighter may be the  headline act but many of the precursors  that made street fighter 2 the marquee  title it is are here additional content  includes puzzle fighter a game mode  which combined combat with tetris levels  of puzzle addiction fans of fighting  games will get a kick out of all the  extras including artwork and renowned  music tracks i know it's not one for  everyone but definitely this will be  appealing to fans of fighters over the  ages and there's an online multiplayer  mode which will be the place to find the  best of the best capcom fighting  collection hits you in the face on june  24th on playstation xbox pc and switch  so that's it a mixed bag of aaa indie  and a butt ton of free to play games  what you're playing this month i reckon  i'll see you all on fall guys am i right  i'm adam you're awesome be sure to leave  a dead joke and i'll see you next time

